WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.581
Threat hunting is not magic and it is not guesswork.

00:00:04.581 --> 00:00:08.166
Effective hunters combine curiosity, analytical thinking, technical knowledge,

00:00:08.166 --> 00:00:12.200
understanding of attacker behaviors, and familiarity with organizational environments.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.785
Hunting complements SIEM operations, EDR investigations, incident response,

00:00:15.785 --> 00:00:18.025
threat intelligence, and detection engineering.

00:00:18.025 --> 00:00:20.714
It does not replace those capabilities.

00:00:20.714 --> 00:00:21.364
Instead,

00:00:21.364 --> 00:00:28.086
it helps teams move from only reacting to alerts toward actively searching for hidden threats.

00:00:28.086 --> 00:00:33.015
A healthy hunting discipline values evidence, documentation, repeatable methods, and feedback.

00:00:33.015 --> 00:00:38.841
Hunters should be able to explain the hypothesis, data sources, search approach, findings,

00:00:38.841 --> 00:00:41.530
confidence level, and recommended next steps.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:46.011
Over time, a mature hunting capability improves resilience, detection quality,

00:00:46.011 --> 00:00:47.356
and operational awareness.

00:00:47.356 --> 00:00:52.733
It helps organizations learn what normal looks like, where visibility is weak,

00:00:52.733 --> 00:00:55.220
and where defenders should improve controls.
